WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0113: a replayed BG3 click carries the modifier keys held on it.
A Shift-click in WoW's quest log never watched the quest (playtest): WoW's handlers read
IsShiftKeyDown from benilla's own keyboard, which hears BG3's keys only while WoW's chat box is
typing (patch 0008), so every click forwarded from BG3 was a plain one. bg3input.bin may be BGI3
(40 bytes: BGI2's fields, the newest click's modifiers at 32 as bits 1 Shift, 2 Ctrl, 4 Alt, the seq
again at 36; WorldMode.lua writes it); the replay presses those keys on benilla's keyboard with the
button and lets go of them the frame after the button's release, once OnClick has run. BGI1 and BGI2
still decode (no modifiers). The pointer log line names the modifiers.
